      "projects": [
        {
          "title": "File Type Detection using Content-based and ML Technique",
          "subtitle": "Mar 2016 - Mar 2016",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with University of Southern California"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- Developed a content-based and machine learning technique that used Byte Frequency Distribution of files for file type detection.\n\n- Worked on developing a deep neural network to provide model files for Apache Tika in order to boost its accuracy in file type detection.\n\n- Provided scaffolding for leveraging other ML techniques for file type detection."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "TMDBApi (Android Library)",
          "subtitle": "Jan 2016 - Present",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with Udacity"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- Created an open source android library for ingesting the movies db api. \n\n- Used libraries such as Retrofit, Gson and JavaRx for creating a production level library that helps interact with functionality of TheMoviesDBApi\n\n- Developed Unit test cases for major functionality in the library. Also, handled various exceptions thrown by TMDBApi. Deployed the library to jcenter Repository and awaiting maven central synch.\n\n- Developers can simply build the plugin through gradle command:\n  compile 'com.rahulravindran:tmdbapi:0.1.1'\n"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Creating Customer Segments",
          "subtitle": "Dec 2015 - Dec 2015",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with Udacity"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- Explored a dataset that refers to clients of a wholesale distributor. It included the annual spending in monetary units (m.u.) on diverse product categories.\n\n- Analysed the possible outcomes of PCA and ICA on the data and built exploratory graphs to communicate the results.\n\n- Employed PCA to reduce the dimensionality of data and captured almost 88% of the variability in the dataset. Constructed Gaussian Mixture Model and visualised the cluster of customer segments using sklearn and python.\n\n- Successfully employed unsupervised learning algorithms to come up with a decision boundary and build customer segments. The end product provides a basis for segmenting customers and provides a platform to employ A/B tests to enhance profits."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Popular Movies Application",
          "subtitle": "Dec 2015 - Dec 2015",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with Udacity"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Developed an android app that consumes \"TheMoviesDB\" API. Following are some of the features of the application:\n\n-Dicover movies with high popularity, vote count and highest rating.\n- Watch Trailers\n- Read Reviews\n\nThe application makes use of some of the best practices using libraries such as\n- Picasso\n- Dagger\n- Retrofit\n\nSome of the highlights of the application is a feature toggle driven development which lets uses turn on and off some of the important aspects of the application.\n"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Student Intervention System",
          "subtitle": "Dec 2015 - Dec 2015",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with Udacity"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- The aim of the project was to devise a student intervention system that lets school officials identify students who are likely to not pass the final exam and intervene accordingly to help these students.\n \n- The objective of the school was to achieve a graduation rate of 95% from 67%. I built a supervised prediction model and performed the following activities to help achieve the school objective:\n\n- Identified the class of problem, separated features from target labels, added dummy variables for computation of predictive models and cleaned data.\n\n- Trained various supervised learning models v.i.z decision tree, random forest, SVM and NBC on the data and compared each of the model performance.\n\n- Tuned and increase performance on Support Vector Machine that resulted in a final F1 score of 0.853. Thus, the final model could accurately identify students who needed help for graduation with an accuracy of 85.3%."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "CSI VESIT Android Application",
          "subtitle": "Dec 2013 - Dec 2013",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Developed an android application for CSI VESIT, features include extensive feed parsing and caching, developed a library to load image faster using cache effectively and also internal sd card storage. \n\nIt is being extensively used by CSI members to get information regarding day to day events. Currently, the application has more than 1000 downloads."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Virtual Stock Market",
          "subtitle": "Sep 2013 - Sep 2013",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Created and maintained a web application on stock market that simulated an actual online stock trading website, This application was conducted as an event by CSI-VESIT and gained a huge amount of success.\n\nThe event was conducted for a period of 3 days and witnessed more than 400 members playing it. It also had more than 0.2 million page views."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Train a smart cab how to drive",
          "subtitle": "Dec 2015 - Jan 2016",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with Udacity"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- Using pygame, developed a reinforcement learning agent for a smart cab that needs to drop off its passenger to the goal state in the shortest time possible.\n\n- Came up with two possible agents one being a naive random walk agent and the other implementing the q-leanrning strategy.\n\n- Developed an algorithm to tweak when the agent needs to explore and when it needs to exploit using the q-learning policy it has developed based on the time left to drop off the passenger.\n\n- The agent performed well in most of the trials it was subjected to. Currently it is being tweaked to learn a definite policy by training it for almost 100 trials."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Big Data Analytics For Behaviour Profiling Using Web Usage History",
          "subtitle": "Jun 2014 - Mar 2015",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "- Traditional approaches to behavior profiling involves psychometric evaluations. We build on the idea of using web usage history to do the same, as people’s personalities tends to effect the choice of the websites they visit. \n\n- Using psychological models, we provide users constructive insights into their personalities and also provide career choices."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
